6,A Trans superstar of South Pacific music- I'm Moshanty,https://www.losangelesblade.com/2020/12/15/a-trans-superstar-of-south-pacific-music-im-moshanty/,"August 27, 2021 - At an early age, Moshanty grew up with parents who were pastors, and although one might jump to the conclusion that pastors in Papua New Guinea might be against Moshanty coming out as trans, the documentary shows her parents as being caring and loving. Moshanty’s mother says, “The scriptures say “do not judge.” Moshanty commented on people preaching hate by saying, “If there is no love, what’s the point of preaching about love on the pulpit if you have all that hate in you?” · Moshanty capitalized on her voice by becoming a musician and songwriter.",Magi,Trans-New Guinea
7,"Sacred Flute Music From New Guinea: Madang / Windim Mabu – 2 x CD (Compilation, Reissue, Remastered), 2016 [r8445385] | Discogs",https://www.discogs.com/release/8445385-Various-Sacred-Flute-Music-From-New-Guinea-Madang-Windim-Mabu,"April 20, 2025 - Copies of the master tapes are in the Institute of Papua New Guinea Studies, Port Moresby. Ragnar Johnson thanks the Canadian I.D.R.C. for supporting his anthropological research. Thanks to Dave Hunt for transferring the original magnetic tape recordings onto digital media and to Stephen O'Malley, David Toop,and Evan Parker for assistance. CD1 originally released on LP 1977 as !Quartz 001 (Sacred Flute Music From New Guinea : Madang) and CD2 1979 as !Quartz 002 (Windim Mambu.",Magi,Trans-New Guinea
8,Papua New Guinea-Music - Online education for kids,https://www.allaroundthisworld.com/learn/oceania-and-the-pacific-islands/papua-new-guinea-2/papua-new-guinea-music/,"October 16, 2016 - From the video description: “O-Shen is an American White boy who grew up in the Morobe Provice of my homeland Papua New Guinea. This is for all you heart broken island boys. Wan fit mangi stret!” ... Argentina–Tango! ... Kyrgyzstan — Manas…YAY! ... Lesson 9: St. Lucia · St. Lucia–Overview · St. Lucia–Music",Magi,Trans-New Guinea
9,Sacred Flute Music From New Guinea: Madang / Windim Mabu | Ragnar Johnson assisted by Jessica Mayer | Ideologic Organ,https://ideologicorgan.bandcamp.com/album/sacred-flute-music-from-new-guinea-madang-windim-mabu,"April 28, 2025 - SOMA024 Sacred flutes are blown (""Windim Mambu'') to make the cries of spirits by adult men in the Madang region of Papua New Guinea. Pairs of long bamboo male and female flutes are played for ceremonies in the coastal villages near the Ramu River.",Magi,Trans-New Guinea
